  "summary_en": "Vietnam's Law on Artificial Intelligence (No. 134/2025/QH15), effective 1 March 2026. It sets a three-tier risk classification, transparency and labelling duties, incident reporting, conformity assessment for high-risk systems, deployer liability, a sandbox, national AI infrastructure, a development fund and an ethics framework. It excludes defence and security uses.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Risk classification into high, medium and low; providers self-classify and notify the Ministry of Science and Technology for medium and high risk",
   "High-risk systems require conformity assessment, human oversight design, technical documentation and logs",
   "Transparency duties: disclose AI interaction, machine-readable marking and labelling of synthetic content",
   "Deployer compensates for damage from high-risk systems even when lawfully operated, with a right of recourse; insurance encouraged",
   "Controlled sandbox, National AI Development Fund, national AI infrastructure and ethics framework; effective 1 March 2026 with 12-18 month transition"
  ],
